      {
        "title": "Show HN: bouncemarket – a live prediction market game for a bouncing ball",
        "link": "https://bouncemarket.minhanhday.com/",
        "description": "<p>a ball will fall. trade on where it lands.<p>I made this game! Some technical details:<p>The entire drop of the ball is simulated server-side, then streamed to each client as server-sent events with a small buffer. Every drop is deterministic from its starting position, so rounds can be replayed exactly for later analysis, but tiny variations in starting position can change the ultimate outcome.<p>There's some AI traders to keep the market moving, but they drop out in any round that has more than five people. They operate using a naive set of rules that I wrote for them, so they're not too hard to beat -- it's when the market is full of real people that it gets tricky.<p>Curious to get feedback on anything you would change, and especially whether the mechanics were clear right away or not.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50667726\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50667726</a></p>\n<p>Points: 285</p>\n<p># Comments: 87</p>",
        "pubDate": "Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:01:50 +0000",
        "guid": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50667726"
      },
      {
        "title": "Show HN: I restored Palm's last device, and brought its OS to other platforms",
        "link": "https://www.webosarchive.org/pivot/2026/11/27/the-story-so-far/",
        "description": "<p>webOS Community Edition 3.2.0 is the first OTA Update for Palm/HP's TouchPad, modernizing a 15-year old device. Lunacy is its sibling: the webOS experience, and apps, on Android. Luna DE is a developer tool that brings the webOS app contract to Mac, Windows and Linux as a SDK-compatible Electron app.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50667452\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50667452</a></p>\n<p>Points: 44</p>\n<p># Comments: 14</p>",
